    "body": "Escalation to `effort:max`. No code is pushed. The claim is released.\n\nFindings:\n- The WCS is stored as a `Location` on the `Wcs` entity: a position and a unit quaternion (`crates/app/src/schema.rs`). A quaternion cannot store a mirror. A flip needs a new schema field (a sign for each axis) and a new project-file key.\n- Toolpath generation, simulation and the gouge checks use only the WCS translation. The CL stream is in the setup frame. The post scripts subtract `OriginX/Y/Z` and do nothing more (16 scripts in `assets/posts/`).\n- The post refuses a rotated WCS by name (`crates/app/src/posting_wcs_rotation.rs`, from #315). Generation refuses a WCS whose Z is tilted (`crates/app/src/setup_wcs_tilt.rs`, #1510). The work to carry a WCS rotation into the toolpath is still open as #760.\n- A flip is a larger change than a rotation. It makes a left-handed frame. The post must change the sign of the coordinates on the flipped axis, swap `G2`/`G3` and the sign of the arc centre words, and swap `G41`/`G42`. A Z flip also changes the tool axis sign, the heights, the retract direction and the canned cycle R and Z planes. This must be correct in every post script, or the engine must bake it into the stream before the scripts. The `operation/frame.rs` frame contract (\"three coordinate systems, never a fourth\") must also change.\n- This is new frame design across the post engine, all post scripts, the verifier and the simulation. That is `effort:max` by the AGENTS.md table.\n\nRecommended split (for the next tier or the maintainer):\n1. `effort:high`: store a flip for each axis, add the undoable command, the three buttons and the MCP tool. The post and generation refuse a flipped WCS by name, as the #315 clause does for a rotation. No posted output changes.\n2. `effort:max`: carry the flip into the posted program, with golden NC tests for arcs and cutter compensation. This can share the frame work of #760.\n\nThe worktree and the local branch `issue/1649-wcs-flip-axes` are removed. The branch was not pushed.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
