    "updated_at": "2026-11-17T22:23:32Z",
    "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-17:\n\n> bug; WCS54, X flipped - posting and generating are refused until the flip is cleared..  the ability to flip axis from a positive to negative is fundamental and should not be blocked.. posting and generation should take it into consideration rather..\n\nReading: v0.23.0 stores the flip (#1720, PR #1738) and refuses generation and the post while a flip is set. The maintainer says that this refusal is not acceptable as the final state. Generation and the post must carry the flip.\n\nRules for the work:\n- One flipped axis is a mirror. A mirror changes climb milling into conventional milling and changes the arc direction (G2 / G3) and the cutter compensation side (G41 / G42). The work must handle each of these, or refuse by name the single case that it cannot handle.\n- Two flipped axes are a half turn about the third axis. That case has no mirror.\n- The refusal of #1720 goes only when the flip is carried correctly, with pinning tests for the posted coordinates, the arc directions and the compensation side.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
